    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0647" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v27/pg609"/>

                <head>219. Letter From President Eisenhower to Prime Minister Eden<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d219-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1955-11-19">November 19, 1955</date>.</hi></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Anthony</hi>: It is good to have your
                        thoughts.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d219-f2"/> You are of course right in saying
                    that to keep Germany divided is dangerous business for Europe and the world as
                    well. We have made some progress however at Geneva in impressing this point on
                    the Russians. At the least I believe we have made clearer to everyone that the
                    Soviet policy concerning Germany is designed to preserve the GDR as the keystone
                    of their satellite position rather than Russian security.</p>
                <p>I agree with you that the only real solution to the dangerous situation in the
                    Middle East is an Israel-Arab settlement. The prospects do look brighter at the
                    moment than they have for some time. We must do everything we can to follow
                    through effectively.</p>
                <p>With warm regard.</p>
                <p>As ever,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">D.E.</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d219-f3"
                        /></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
